    109 => "An `import` declaration after an item",
    110 =>
        "Nested more than 1,000 levels deep (grammar.md §2.2: blocks, statements, types, patterns, unary operands, and each link of an operator, call or member chain). The rest of the file is not parsed",
    200 => "Name not found (variable, function, or built-in member)",
    201 =>
        "Item defined twice in the package (a library item's name is not a clash since ADR 0075 §5: the package's item shadows it), or a C name declared twice by C functions, exports or `@repr` types, even in different packages (`type-system.md` §28.2, §28.5, ADR 0081 §2.2)",
    202 => "Parameter declared twice",
    203 => "Local redeclares a local or parameter in scope (no shadowing of locals)",
    204 => "Unknown type name",
    205 => "Type mismatch against the expected type",
    206 => "Integer literal out of range for its type",
    207 =>
        "Operator not applicable to the operand types (includes mixed types, signed bitwise ops, negating unsigned values; `==` on an enum with payloads, or on slices or arrays of floats or structs, ADR 0072; a field without `==` under `@derive(Equal)`, ADR 0087 §2.3; `+` on views outside a constant or static initialiser, ADR 0087 §2.7)",
    208 => "`as` conversion that can lose information",
    209 => "Wrong number of arguments",
    210 => "Not callable, or a function or built-in used as a value",
    211 =>
